#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%(model)s does not have approvals turned on in %(package)s, so there is "
"nothing here to change. A gate another module wrote is that module's to "
"edit."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%(model)s has a %(method)s method in its class that approvals did not write,"
" or that has been changed since. Turning approvals on, changing them or "
"turning them off would replace or remove it, so move it below the builder's "
"block, or make the change by hand."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%(model)s has no field called %(field)s, and approvals are a gate on a state"
" change. Add a status field first."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%(model)s has no such value for %(field)s: %(unknown)s. A rule naming a "
"value the field does not have never fires, which looks exactly like "
"approvals being switched off."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%(model)s is not a class the builder can rewrite in %(package)s "
"(%(reason)s), so there is nowhere safe to write the approval gate. Fix the "
"file, or add the gate to it by hand."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid "%s already has approvals turned on."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval_surface.py:0
msgid "%s approves"
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%s cannot be both a state that needs approving into and the cancelled state,"
" which drops the approvals asked for."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"%s is on both sides of the transition, so there is no moment at which "
"approval could be asked for."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-javascript
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/static/src/console_items.js:0
msgid ""
"A rule names the reviewer and the records it covers. Rules you add are "
"written to security/<model>_approval.xml."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval_surface.py:0
msgid ""
"An approval rule gates a state change, and the model has to carry the gate "
"first."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"An approval rule gates a state change, and the model has to carry the gate "
"first: turn approvals on from the builder, then come back here to say who "
"approves what."
msgstr ""

#. module: app_builder_approval
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/app_builder_approval/models/builder_approval.py:0
msgid ""
"Approval would not be asked for from: %(uncovered)s. %(field)s is an "
"ordinary writable field, so a record could be moved there first and on into "
"%(to)s with no approval at all. Leave the origin states empty to gate every "
"way in, or add the missing ones."
msgstr ""

